---
// <main> content ported from skatelog-web 8e7af91:web/support.html. Only hrefs
// change (support.html#contact becomes /support#contact); the text must stay
// as approved, and `node scripts/check-dist.mjs --source <dir>` compares it.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ContactForm from '../components/ContactForm.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Sk8tics Support"
  description="Help with Sk8tics — coach links, competition import, scoring, and how to get in touch." current="support"
>

  <p class="eyebrow">Support</p>
  <h1>Something not working?</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Use the <a href="#contact">contact form</a> below.
    It is read by the person who built the app. Tell us what you were doing and
    what happened instead, and it helps to say which phone you are on.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions that come up</h2>

  <h3>How does a coach get access to my log?</h3>
  <p>
    Either side can start it &mdash; you can invite a coach, or a coach can
    search for you by name and invite you. Nothing is shared until the other
    side accepts. You can end the link at any time from the Coaches screen, and
    access stops the moment you do.
  </p>

  <h3>My competition isn&rsquo;t showing up when I search</h3>
  <p>
    Two common reasons. Results for an event that has just finished can take
    several days to be published &mdash; the app can only read what is on the
    website. And STAR 1&ndash;4 events often list a results link that never
    receives a file, which is a quirk of how those events are published rather
    than a problem with the search.
  </p>
  <p>
    Searching is scoped to a season. If you are looking for an older skate,
    choose the right season first.
  </p>

  <h3>A score in the app doesn&rsquo;t match the printed protocol</h3>
  <p>
    An imported competition uses the base values printed on the sheet, so it
    should match exactly. Tell us if it does not &mdash; that is a bug and we
    want it.
  </p>
  <p>
    A <em>run-through</em> score is different: it uses the current ISU scale of
    values to work out what a programme would be worth. If a number there looks
    wrong, send us the element code through the <a href="#contact">contact form</a>
    and we will check it against the communication.
  </p>

  <h3>Can I use it for ice dance or pairs?</h3>
  <p>
    Yes. Singles, ice dance and pairs each have their own scale of values.
    Discipline is chosen when you sign up and decides which one your scores are
    read against, so it cannot be changed from inside the app &mdash; use the
    <a href="#contact">contact form</a> and we will change it for you.
  </p>

  <h3>I&rsquo;m not getting notifications</h3>
  <p>
    Check the account sheet in the app first, then your phone&rsquo;s own
    notification setting for Sk8tics. Notifications tell you that a score
    arrived, never what it was &mdash; a lock screen is not a private place for
    a mark.
  </p>

  <h3>Is it on Android?</h3>
  <p>
    It is in closed testing on Google Play now. If you would like to be a
    tester, send us a message through the <a href="#contact">contact form</a>
    and we will send you the opt-in link.
  </p>

  <h2>Deleting your account</h2>
  <p>
    Do it yourself in the app: tap <strong>Account</strong> at the top of any
    screen, scroll to the bottom, type your username where it says
    <strong>Type <em>your username</em> to confirm</strong>, then tap
    <strong>Delete my account</strong>. It is immediate and cannot be undone.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you can't sign in, use the <a href="#contact">contact form</a> with the
    email address on the account. We will reply to that address to confirm
    before we delete anything.
  </p>

  <ContactForm />

</Base>
